   192	Because dotted result-directory names are not normal Python package names, the
   193	reliable command-line checks from the repository root are:
   194	
   195	```bash
   196	python3 results/0902.4670/gen_0902_4670.py
   197	python3 scripts/harden.py results/0902.4670/gen_0902_4670.py
   198	bash scripts/emit.sh 0902.4670 20 easy
   199	```
   200	
   201	## Caveats
   202	
   203	The family becomes easy immediately when the norm invariant is recognized;
   204	that is intentional Track-B behavior, not evidence for average-case class-group
   205	hardness. The 0/250,000 guess figure is empirical and is conditioned on the
   206	freely deducible first-sign normalization; uniqueness additionally proves that
   207	the uniform probability is exactly `1/2^30`, but neither figure models solvers
   208	with number-theoretic priors. The inverse construction guarantees a unique
   209	normalized answer in this parameter range, while
   210	arbitrary relations from the paper need not be unique.
   211	
   212	The attacks do not include generic CAS class-group software, lattice reduction,
   213	or a learned pattern detector. A CAS would solve these instances, as would the
   214	178-operation compact route, and both are consistent with Track B. The tested
   215	heuristics were all-positive orientation, smallest oriented roots, greedy
   216	prefix CRT, a 256-choice by-hand window, and 2,048 random restarts. Finally, no
   217	external model hardness claim is currently supported: the OpenRouter quota
   218	failure must be cleared and all three bare attempts must produce real replies
   219	before this family can be submitted as hardened.

